"SustainabilitySustainabilityiFinancial RiskAvailable resources are expected to be exhausted in Nov 2026, before break even in Jun 2027. Additional funding, lower costs, earlier revenue, higher prices or greater volume may be needed.Expected Monthly Revenuei£11,699at the normal levelBreak-Even Revenuei£11,206a monthExpected Break EveniJun 2027Month 27 of the planFinancial ExhaustioniNov 2026Month 20 of the planSustainability Bufferin/afunds run out before break evenExpected Monthly Revenue£11,699Break-Even Revenue£11,206Break-Even Activity≈ 9.6 products a month (Homeware Collection)≈ 30.7 participants a month (Weaving Workshops)≈ 2.9 projects a month (Bespoke Commissions)≈ 2.9 products a month (Trade Collection)Expected Break EvenJun 2027Financial ExhaustionNov 2026Sustainability Buffern/a!Financial Risk. Available resources are expected to be exhausted in Nov 2026, before break even in Jun 2027. Additional funding, lower costs, earlier revenue, higher prices or greater volume may be needed.Based on the current assumptions only. These are estimates, not guarantees or financial advice.Stress TestiThe plan does not hold even as planned: cash falls £18,074 short in May 2027. The hardest case, all four together, falls £56,087 short.Counting the £26,000 being sought as if it arrives as planned, its repayments included.CaseBreak EvenLowest CashResultAs plannedJun 2027-£18,074, May 2027£18,074 shortSales 20% lowerNot reached-£23,175, May 2027£23,175 shortRevenue 3 months laterSep 2027-£32,824, May 2027£32,824 shortCosts 10% higherNot reached-£23,420, May 2027£23,420 shortCustomers pay 1 month laterJun 2027-£27,229, May 2027£27,229 shortAll four togetherNot reached-£56,087, Mar 2028£56,087 shortWhat It Would TakeiTo keep cash above zero through the plan, with the £26,000 being sought, any one of these would do:£18,074 more funding, by Nov 2026Prices 124% higherSales 166% higherCosts 47% lower, founders' pay asideRevenue starting 4 months earlierEach on its own, with everything else as planned; a mix of smaller changes can do the same.Back‹›Back
[fields] "
`;

