E9 5LN | 03/02/2025 | 04/01/2025 | Lumen & Loom Studio Ltd is a London-based textile design studio, founded in 2026 by Maya Chen, Oliver Grant and Priya Shah and based at a shared workshop in Hackney Wick, East London. We design and handweave sustainable home textiles (cushions, throws, table linen and wall hangings) from British wool, organic cotton and recycled yarns. Alongside our own collection we run small-group weaving workshops and take bespoke commissions for interior designers and boutique hotels."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile philosophy-manifesto 1`] = `
"Philosophy & ManifestoPhilosophyiWe believe the things we live with shape how we live. A well-made textile, repaired and kept for decades, teaches us to care for what we own. Our work is a small, practical argument for slowness: fewer, better things, made close to home by people you can meet.ManifestoiWe stand for things made slowly and kept for a lifetime. We stand for knowing who made your cushion and where the wool came from. We stand against throwaway homeware, hidden supply chains and craft reduced to a style. Come and see how it's made. Better still, come and make it with us.Back‹›Back
[fields] We believe the things we live with shape how we live. A well-made textile, repaired and kept for decades, teaches us to care for what we own. Our work is a small, practical argument for slowness: fewer, better things, made close to home by people you can meet. | We stand for things made slowly and kept for a lifetime. We stand for knowing who made your cushion and where the wool came from. We stand against throwaway homeware, hidden supply chains and craft reduced to a style. Come and see how it's made. Better still, come and make it with us."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile positioning 1`] = `
"Core Market PositioningCore Market PositioningiSeller & Buyer Relationshipi 2 maxB2C (Business-to-Consumer)B2B (Business-to-Business)Buyer's Life-Stagei 2 maxStudents / Young AdultsWorkers / ProfessionalsSeniorsBuyer's category (B2C)iDirect BuyersProxy BuyersDual-Intent BuyersAudience Specialisation & Scalei 2 maxSolopreneurs & FreelancersStartups & SMBsMid-MarketEnterprise or Public SectorBuyer's category (B2B)iDirect BuyersProxy BuyersDual-Intent BuyersPurposei 2 maxLearning & DevelopmentEntertainment & EnjoymentProductivity & EfficiencyBusiness Growth & PerformanceEveryday Needs & ConvenienceHealth, Care & WellbeingGifting & AppreciationSocial Connection & RelationshipsCreation & ExpressionProtection & Risk ReductionCompliance & ObligationsNotesiFor design-conscious Londoners and interior professionals who want homeware with a story, Lumen & Loom is an independent textile studio that makes every piece by hand in London from traceable, low-impact yarns. Each piece is made in a small batch, can be repaired for life, and comes with the name of the weaver who made it, and our studio is open: customers can learn to weave with us. Back‹›Back
[fields] For design-conscious Londoners and interior professionals who want homeware with a story, Lumen & Loom is an independent textile studio that makes every piece by hand in London from traceable, low-impact yarns. Each piece is made in a small batch, can be repaired for life, and comes with the name of the weaver who made it, and our studio is open: customers can learn to weave with us. "
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile values-principles 1`] = `
"Values & PrinciplesValuesi1.Craft over speed2.Honesty about materials and prices3.Care for people and planet4.Openness: share skills, not secrets5.Community before scalePrinciplesi1.Every yarn we use is traceable to its farm or mill.2.We pay our makers and suppliers a London Living Wage or better.3.We repair anything we have made, for life.4.We never discount to clear stock; we make to order instead.5.We decide by consensus of the three founders on anything that affects people or materials.Back‹›Back
