exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile mission-vision 1`] = `
"Mission & VisionMissioniTo give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity.VisioniA future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in.What will your business be when your Vision comes true?i 3 maxServing a large, growing customer baseLoved & recommended by its customersOffering a strong, growing rangeProfitable & paying its own wayKnown & trusted in its fieldRunning smoothly with a strong teamWorking closely with strong partnersWhere will your customers be?iIn my city / townIn my state / regionAcross my countryIn several countriesWorldwideToday: In my state / region (NYC Service Firms)Back‹›Back
[fields] To give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity. | A future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile organization 1`] = `
"OrganisationOrganisationi1.OrganisationOrganisation NameCountryUnited States of AmericaSelect a country, for example United States of AmericaAustraliaCanadaIrelandNew ZealandUnited KingdomUnited States of AmericaOtherStateNew YorkSelect a stateAlabamaAlaskaArizonaArkansasCaliforniaColoradoConnecticutDelawareDistrict of ColumbiaFloridaGeorgiaHawaiiIdahoIllinoisIndianaIowaKansasKentuckyLouisianaMaineMarylandMassachusettsMichiganMinnesotaMississippiMissouriMontanaNebraskaNevadaNew HampshireNew JerseyNew MexicoNew YorkNorth CarolinaNorth DakotaOhioOklahomaOregonPennsylvaniaRhode IslandSouth CarolinaSouth DakotaTennesseeTexasUtahVermontVirginiaWashingtonWest VirginiaWisconsinWyomingOtherAddress120 Clinton Street, Suite 3R Brooklyn 11201Legal FormiSole ProprietorshipSelect a legal formSole ProprietorshipGeneral PartnershipLimited Partnership (LP)Limited Liability Company (LLC)C CorporationS CorporationOpening DateiActivitiesiPrimaryNAICS 541512NotesiQuillfield Automation is a one-person automation studio in Brooklyn, New York, founded in 2026 by Jordan Ellis. We design and build AI-assisted workflow automations for small professional-services firms: law, accounting, architecture and marketing firms of 5 to 50 staff. We provide three services. The AI Workflow Audit finds the repetitive work worth automating. The Automation Build puts the chosen workflows into daily use. The Automation Care Retainer keeps them running, secure and up to date.Back‹›Back
[fields] Quillfield Automation | 120 Clinton Street, Suite 3R
Brooklyn
11201 | 02/01/2027 | Quillfield Automation is a one-person automation studio in Brooklyn, New York, founded in 2026 by Jordan Ellis. We design and build AI-assisted workflow automations for small professional-services firms: law, accounting, architecture and marketing firms of 5 to 50 staff. We provide three services. The AI Workflow Audit finds the repetitive work worth automating. The Automation Build puts the chosen workflows into daily use. The Automation Care Retainer keeps them running, secure and up to date."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile philosophy-manifesto 1`] = `
"Philosophy & ManifestoPhilosophyiWe believe technology should serve people's working day, not reshape it around a tool. The best automation is quiet: it removes a chore, works every time and is easy to understand. We would rather automate one workflow well than ten badly. And we believe clients should always own, and understand, what we build for them.ManifestoiWe stand for small firms having the same smart tools as large ones. We stand for automation that people understand, own and trust. We stand against hype, black-box systems and contracts that lock clients in. We stand against software that replaces people's judgement without anyone checking it. Everything we build exists for one reason: to give people back time for the work they chose their profession for.Back‹›Back
[fields] We believe technology should serve people's working day, not reshape it around a tool. The best automation is quiet: it removes a chore, works every time and is easy to understand. We would rather automate one workflow well than ten badly. And we believe clients should always own, and understand, what we build for them. | We stand for small firms having the same smart tools as large ones. We stand for automation that people understand, own and trust. We stand against hype, black-box systems and contracts that lock clients in. We stand against software that replaces people's judgement without anyone checking it. Everything we build exists for one reason: to give people back time for the work they chose their profession for."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile positioning 1`] = `
"Early PositioningEarly PositioningiSeller & Buyer RelationshipiB2C (Business-to-Consumer)B2B (Business-to-Business)Audience Specialisation & ScaleiSolopreneurs & FreelancersStartups & SMBsMid-MarketEnterprise or Public SectorBuyer's categoryiDirect BuyersProxy BuyersDual-Intent BuyersPurposeiLearning & DevelopmentEntertainment & EnjoymentProductivity & EfficiencyBusiness Growth & PerformanceEveryday Needs & ConvenienceHealth, Care & WellbeingGifting & AppreciationSocial Connection & RelationshipsCreation & ExpressionProtection & Risk ReductionCompliance & ObligationsNotesiFor owners and office managers of small professional-services firms who know automation could help but have no technical staff, Quillfield Automation is a hands-on automation partner in the small-business IT and consulting market. Clients work directly with the person who designs and builds their system, at fixed project prices, and we map the workflow first, build on the firm's existing software, document every step and stay on to maintain it.Back‹›Back
[fields] For owners and office managers of small professional-services firms who know automation could help but have no technical staff, Quillfield Automation is a hands-on automation partner in the small-business IT and consulting market. Clients work directly with the person who designs and builds their system, at fixed project prices, and we map the workflow first, build on the firm's existing software, document every step and stay on to maintain it."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile values-principles 1`] = `
"Values & PrinciplesValuesi1.Clarity over cleverness2.Reliability in everything we deliver3.Honesty about what AI can and cannot do4.Respect for client data and privacy5.Long-term partnershipPrinciplesi1.We map and measure a workflow before we automate it.2.We quote fixed prices and agree the scope in writing.3.We build on the client's existing tools wherever we can.4.Every automation that affects clients or money has a named person who checks it.5.We document every build so the client could run it without us.6.We never put client data into a new tool without the client's written approval.7.We turn down work we cannot deliver well.Back‹›Back
[fields] Clarity over cleverness | Reliability in everything we deliver | Honesty about what AI can and cannot do | Respect for client data and privacy | Long-term partnership | We map and measure a workflow before we automate it. | We quote fixed prices and agree the scope in writing. | We build on the client's existing tools wherever we can. | Every automation that affects clients or money has a named person who checks it. | We document every build so the client could run it without us. | We never put client data into a new tool without the client's written approval. | We turn down work we cannot deliver well."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 1. Definition 1`] = `
"…Saving…AutoFocusSearchWorkbookNotesSettingsQuillfield Automation1. Identity System — 1. Definition & Purpose1. DefinitionOrganisationQuillfield AutomationSole Proprietorship120 Clinton Street, Suite 3RBrooklyn 11201Early PositioningStartups & SMBsDirectProductivity & EfficiencyFounders & OwnershipJordan Ellis2. PurposeMission &VisionTo give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity.A future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in.Values &Principles1. Clarity over cleverness2. Reliability in everything we deliver3. Honesty about what AI can and cannot do4. Respect for client data and privacy5. Long-term partnership1. We map and measure a workflow before we automate it.2. We quote fixed prices and agree the scope in writing.3. We build on the client's existing tools wherever we can.4. Every automation that affects clients or money has a named person who checks it.5. We document every build so the client could run it without us.6. We never put client data into a new tool without the client's written approval.7. We turn down work we cannot deliver well.Philosophy &ManifestoWe believe technology should serve people's working day, not reshape it around a tool. The best automation is quiet: it removes a chore, works every time and is easy to understand. We would rather automate one workflow well than ten badly. And we believe clients should always own, and understand, what we build for them.We stand for small firms having the same smart tools as large ones. We stand for automation that people understand, own and trust. We stand against hype, black-box systems and contracts that lock clients in. We stand against software that replaces people's judgement without anyone checking it. Everything we build exists for one reason: to give people back time for the work they chose their profession for.‹PagesIntroduction1. Definition & Purpose: defined2. Legal Entity: defined›Back
[fields] "
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 2. Purpose > tile legal-entity-founders 1`] = `
"Founders & OwnershipFounders & OwnershipiNameJordan EllisCapital ($)Rolesi1.Founder & Automation Consultant2.Solutions ArchitectRelevant Industry ExperienceiNine years in IT and automation for professional-services firms: IT consultant at a New York managed-services provider serving law and accounting firms, then solutions architect at a workflow-software company, designing integrations for its small-business customers.Management ExperienceiLed a team of four implementation consultants at the workflow-software company for three years, owning a $600,000 annual services budget and around 40 customer rollouts a year.Key Achievementsi1.Designed an invoice-intake automation that cut a 30-person accounting firm's processing time by 70% (from 12 to 3.5 hours a week) in 20242.Delivered 120 customer integrations at the workflow-software company, 96% of them on time, 2022–2025Skills, Expertise & Qualificationsi1.BS in Information SystemsDegree / QualificationTypeSkillProfessional / Technical ExpertiseDegree / QualificationCertificationLicenceMembership / Other Credential2.Certified in Microsoft Power Platform and ZapierCertificationTypeSkillProfessional / Technical ExpertiseDegree / QualificationCertificationLicenceMembership / Other Credential3.Workflow mapping and process designProfessional / Technical ExpertiseTypeSkillProfessional / Technical ExpertiseDegree / QualificationCertificationLicenceMembership / Other Credential4.Python and API integrationSkillTypeSkillProfessional / Technical ExpertiseDegree / QualificationCertificationLicenceMembership / Other Credential5.Data security and access control for client recordsProfessional / Technical ExpertiseTypeSkillProfessional / Technical ExpertiseDegree / QualificationCertificationLicenceMembership / Other CredentialBack‹›Back
[fields] Jordan Ellis | Founder & Automation Consultant | Solutions Architect | Nine years in IT and automation for professional-services firms: IT consultant at a New York managed-services provider serving law and accounting firms, then solutions architect at a workflow-software company, designing integrations for its small-business customers. | Led a team of four implementation consultants at the workflow-software company for three years, owning a $600,000 annual services budget and around 40 customer rollouts a year. | Designed an invoice-intake automation that cut a 30-person accounting firm's processing time by 70% (from 12 to 3.5 hours a week) in 2024 | Delivered 120 customer integrations at the workflow-software company, 96% of them on time, 2022–2025 | BS in Information Systems | Certified in Microsoft Power Platform and Zapier | Workflow mapping and process design | Python and API integration | Data security and access control for client records"
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 2. Purpose > tile mission-vision 1`] = `
"Mission & VisionMissioniTo give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity.VisioniA future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in.What will your business be when your Vision comes true?i 3 maxServing a large, growing customer baseLoved & recommended by its customersOffering a strong, growing rangeProfitable & paying its own wayKnown & trusted in its fieldRunning smoothly with a strong teamWorking closely with strong partnersWhere will your customers be?iIn my city / townIn my state / regionAcross my countryIn several countriesWorldwideToday: In my state / region (NYC Service Firms)Back‹›Back
[fields] To give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity. | A future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in."
`;

