`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Strategy System › 1. Situation & Direction > tile strategy-foundation-2 1`] = `
"Strategic CompassStrategic CompassiWhat will this period's strategy mainly do?iUse your strengths to seize opportunitiesClose your gaps by seizing opportunitiesWhere will growth come from in this period?i 2 maxYour first customers, won at launchMore sales to the customers you serveNew customers or places for what you offerNew Offerings for the customers you serveNew Offerings for new customersAdd a draftFrom 2027 to 2029, Quillfield moves from a solo launch to a stable business with recurring income. Direction: close the funding gap before the mid-2027 low point, then grow the Care Retainer base until recurring revenue covers the fixed costs. Focus: law and accounting firms of 5 to 50 staff in New York City, the three core services, and repeatable, documented builds. What we will not do: build our own software products, take work outside professional services, chase large enterprise contracts or discount to win work.Back‹›Back
[fields] From 2027 to 2029, Quillfield moves from a solo launch to a stable business with recurring income. Direction: close the funding gap before the mid-2027 low point, then grow the Care Retainer base until recurring revenue covers the fixed costs. Focus: law and accounting firms of 5 to 50 staff in New York City, the three core services, and repeatable, documented builds. What we will not do: build our own software products, take work outside professional services, chase large enterprise contracts or discount to win work."
